LANG tasks v1
# ESR1 Structural Diversity and Redundancy - what must exist for the project to be finished.
# Source of truth: project description (sections 4-10). Language rules: TASK_LANG.md.
# Every task is small (XS <30 min, S <=2 h, M <=half day) and has a machine-checkable chk.
# Path convention: data/ inputs, results/ tables+npy, figures/ png+pml, docs/ text, docs/manuscript/ draft.
# orig = file in the ORIGINAL project folder that already implements it (hint only; port, do not trust).
# who: A data+QC, B structure+redundancy, C chemistry, D comparison+figures+manuscript, ALL.

# ===================== QC / DATA (phase qc) =====================

T Q01 XS run "Query ESR1 PDB IDs"
  help List every X-ray PDB entry for UniProt P03372 (ESR1) from the RCSB search API, one ID per line.
  meta wk=1 who=A ph=qc
  tool requests, RCSB search API
  out data/pdb_ids_esr1.txt
  chk lines data/**/pdb_ids_esr1*.txt >=450
  orig esr_analysis/query_structures.py
  src desc 4.1

T Q02 XS run "Query ESR2 PDB IDs"
  help Same query for UniProt Q92731 (ESR2); this is the validation set (~37-40 entries).
  meta wk=1 who=A ph=qc
  tool requests, RCSB search API
  out data/pdb_ids_esr2.txt
  chk lines data/**/pdb_ids_esr2*.txt >=30
  orig esr_analysis/query_structures.py
  src desc 4.1

T Q03 S run "Download all mmCIF files"
  help Download every ESR1+ESR2 structure as mmCIF into data/raw; skip files already present; record a hash per file.
  meta wk=1 who=A ph=qc
  needs Q01 Q02
  tool requests, hashlib
  out data/raw/*.cif
  chk glob data/raw/**/*.cif >=450
  orig esr_analysis/download_structures.py

T Q17 XS code "Make the download manifest portable (relative paths only)"
  help data/raw/download_manifest.csv stores absolute paths with the local user name. Rewrite the path column as repo-relative (data/raw/XXXX.cif) without re-downloading, and fix the writer so it stays relative.
  meta wk=2 who=A ph=qc
  needs Q03
  out data/raw/download_manifest.csv
  chk csv data/raw/download_manifest.csv rows>=500 cols=pdb_id,download_ok,status,path,source_url nonempty=pdb_id,path uniq=pdb_id
  chk cmd ! grep -q "/home/" data/raw/download_manifest.csv

T Q04 S code "Extract LBD chain per entry (residues 305-550)"
  help Map each entry's receptor chains onto canonical ESR1/ESR2 numbering and keep the ligand-binding domain; record coverage per chain.
  meta wk=1 who=A ph=qc
  needs Q03
  tool biopython
  out results/lbd_chains.csv
  chk csv results/**/lbd*.csv rows>=400 cols=entry_id,chain_id
  orig esr_analysis/extract_lbd.py
  src desc 5.1 step 1

T Q05 S code "Build master metadata CSV"
  help One row per entry: resolution, R-free, mean B, space group, deposit date, depositing authors, ligand ids.
  meta wk=2 who=A ph=qc
  needs Q03
  tool biopython, pandas
  out results/entries.csv
  chk csv results/**/entries*.csv rows>=450 cols=entry_id,resolution,r_free,mean_b,space_group,deposit_date
  orig esr_analysis/extract_metadata.py
  src desc 4.2

T Q06 XS code "Add QC flags (resolution, R-free, B)"
  help Flag resolution >2.5 A, R-free >0.30, mean B >50 A^2; a combined pass needs all three; missing values are not passes. Do not delete failing entries.
  meta wk=2 who=A ph=qc
  needs Q05
  tool pandas
  out results/entries.csv
  chk csv results/**/entries*.csv rows>=450 cols=qc_res,qc_rfree,qc_b,qc_pass
  orig esr_analysis/flag_quality.py
  src desc 4.2

T Q07 XS text "Write QC summary (counts pass/fail per flag)"
  help One short table: how many entries pass each flag and the combined flag, for all entries and for the selected-LBD set.
  meta wk=2 who=A ph=qc
  needs Q06 Q04
  out docs/qc_summary.md
  chk lines docs/qc_summary.md >=8
  chk grep docs/qc_summary.md (?i)R-free

T Q08 S code "Ligand identity table with SMILES"
  help One row per distinct non-water ligand (CCD code) with canonical SMILES from the PDB Chemical Component Dictionary, plus which entries carry it.
  meta wk=2 who=A ph=qc
  needs Q05
  tool requests, RCSB CCD
  out results/ligands.csv
  chk csv results/ligands.csv rows>=300 cols=ligand_id,smiles nonempty=ligand_id uniq=ligand_id
  orig esr_analysis/build_ligand_table.py

T Q09 XS code "Rank ligands by number of entries"
  help Sort ligands by how many entries carry them; this is the worklist for labelling.
  meta wk=2 who=A ph=qc
  needs Q08
  out results/ligands_ranked.csv
  chk csv results/ligands_ranked.csv rows>=300 cols=ligand_id,n_entries nonempty=ligand_id uniq=ligand_id

T Q16 XS code "Flag crystallization additives and ions in the ligand ranking"
  help Add an is_additive column to results/ligands_ranked.csv (ions, buffer and cryoprotectants such as MG, CL, GOL, EDO, SO4, ZN, NA). Keep every row; read ligand_id as text so the real code NA (sodium) stays NA.
  meta wk=2 who=A ph=qc
  needs Q09
  out results/ligands_ranked.csv
  chk csv results/ligands_ranked.csv rows>=300 cols=ligand_id,n_entries,is_additive nonempty=ligand_id,is_additive uniq=ligand_id

T Q18 S code "One ligand of interest per selected chain (drop waters, ions, buffer, cryoprotectants)"
  help For each eligible ESR1 chain, find the non-polymer that sits in the ligand-binding pocket. Use the mmCIF flag pdbx_entity_instance_feature 'SUBJECT OF INVESTIGATION' when present; otherwise keep non-polymers with heavy atoms within 4.5 A of at least 3 pocket residues (M343 L346 T347 A350 E353 W383 L384 L387 M388 L391 R394 F404 M421 I424 F425 L428 G521 H524 L525; put the list in config and cite it). Never count HOH, ions, glycerol, ethylene glycol, PEG, sulfate, phosphate, DMSO, acetate, formate or buffers as the ligand. Keep every chain; a chain with no pocket ligand gets ligand_id empty and status apo_or_unclear. Several pocket ligands: one row each, flag multi. Save the script in scripts/ and read ids with keep_default_na=False.
  meta wk=2 who=A ph=qc
  needs Q04 Q08
  tool biopython or gemmi, numpy
  out scripts/ligand_of_interest.py
  out results/chain_ligand_of_interest.csv
  chk csv results/chain_ligand_of_interest.csv rows>=700 cols=chain_key,entry_id,ligand_id,source,n_pocket_residues,status nonempty=chain_key,status
  chk cmd ! grep -Eq "(^|,)(HOH|MG|CL|NA|K|CA|ZN|NI|GOL|EDO|PEG|SO4|PO4|DMS|ACY|FMT|BME)(,|$)" results/chain_ligand_of_interest.csv
  chk file scripts/ligand_of_interest.py

T Q10 M manual "Label top 30 ligands as agonist / antagonist / SERM (with source)"
  help For the 30 most frequent non-additive ligands (is_additive is false) record the pharmacological class and a citable source (paper or ChEMBL). Unsure = unknown, never guess.
  meta wk=2 who=A ph=qc
  needs Q16 Q18
  out results/ligand_action_labels.csv
  chk csv results/**/ligand_action*.csv rows>=30 cols=ligand_id,action,source
  chk man Human confirms every label has a real source and uncertain ones are marked unknown
  orig results/week6/ligand_action_evidence.csv (14 supported identities so far)
  src desc 3.2

T Q11 M manual "Label next 30 ligands"
  help Same as Q10 for ligands ranked 31-60. Goal: most entries covered by a supported label.
  meta wk=3 who=A ph=qc
  needs Q10
  out results/ligand_action_labels.csv
  chk csv results/**/ligand_action*.csv rows>=60 cols=ligand_id,action,source
  chk man Human confirms sources for the added labels

T Q12 S code "Flag near-duplicate entries"
  help Mark entries with the same ligand, same space group and same depositing group as near-duplicates; this explains part of the redundancy.
  meta wk=2 who=A ph=qc
  needs Q05 Q08
  out results/near_duplicates.csv
  chk csv results/**/near_dup*.csv rows>=1 cols=entry_id,group_id

T Q13 XS fig "Temporal bias: entries deposited per year"
  help Bar chart of deposits per year to check whether recent depositions drive the redundancy.
  meta wk=3 who=A ph=qc
  needs Q05
  tool matplotlib
  out figures/deposits_per_year.png
  chk file figures/**/deposits_per_year*.png

T Q14 S code "QC question 1: do conformational singletons have worse resolution?"
  help Compare resolution and R-free of singleton/rare clusters against the large clusters; a stats line plus one plot.
  meta wk=6 who=A ph=qc
  needs S09 Q06
  out results/qc_outliers.csv
  chk csv results/**/qc_outlier*.csv rows>=1
  chk file docs/qc_outliers.md
  src desc 4.2

T Q15 S code "QC question 2: do high-B entries cluster together or scatter?"
  help Cross-tabulate B-factor flag against structural cluster; report whether high-B entries concentrate in particular clusters.
  meta wk=6 who=A ph=qc
  needs S08 Q06
  out results/qc_bfactor_clusters.csv
  chk csv results/**/qc_bfactor*.csv rows>=1
  src desc 4.2

# ===================== STRUCTURE (phase core) =====================

T S01 S code "Choose and document the reference structure"
  help Pick one reference: QC pass, high LBD coverage, complete core helices and H12, best resolution. Write down why and what its limitations are (engineered substitutions).
  meta wk=2 who=B ph=core
  needs Q04 Q06
  out docs/reference.md
  chk grep docs/reference.md (?i)reference
  chk lines docs/reference.md >=5
  orig choose_reference.py (clean version chose 7NFB chain B model 1)

T S02 M code "Core-helix superposition function (H3,H5,H7,H10; exclude H12)"
  help Kabsch fit on Calpha of residues 340-360, 400-420, 450-470, 500-520 only, so H12 (538-547) stays free to be measured afterwards. Returns core RMSD.
  meta wk=2 who=B ph=core
  needs S01
  tool biopython, numpy
  out esr_analysis/align_structures.py
  chk file esr_analysis/align_structures.py
  chk grep esr_analysis/align_structures.py esr1_core_ranges
  orig esr_analysis/align_structures.py
  src desc 5.1 step 1

T S03 S run "Align every selected chain; log core RMSD per chain"
  help Apply S02 to all selected LBD chains, save fits and a core-RMSD table (a large core RMSD flags a bad fit).
  meta wk=3 who=B ph=core
  needs S02 Q04
  out results/alignment_core_rmsd.csv
  chk csv results/**/align*.csv rows>=300 cols=entry_id,core_rmsd
  orig esr_analysis/align_structures.py

T S04 S run "Pairwise Calpha RMSD matrix (ESR1) - save to disk"
  help N x N RMSD over common LBD Calpha positions after the core fit; save with np.save and never recompute in notebooks.
  meta wk=3 who=B ph=core
  needs S03
  tool numpy
  out results/rmsd_entry.npy
  chk npy results/**/rmsd*.npy square>=300
  orig esr_analysis/calculate_rmsd.py
  src desc 5.1 step 2

T S05 XS code "Save matrix row order (index file)"
  help Ordered list of entry/chain ids matching the matrix rows, so every analysis loads labels without guessing.
  meta wk=3 who=B ph=core
  needs S04
  out results/rmsd_entry_index.csv
  chk csv results/**/rmsd*index*.csv rows>=300
  orig results/current/rmsd_entry_index.txt

T S06 XS text "State the Calpha-only limitation"
  help One paragraph: RMSD uses Calpha only, side-chain rearrangements are not measured; say what that could hide.
  meta wk=3 who=B ph=core
  needs S04
  out docs/limitations.md
  chk grep docs/limitations.md (?i)all-atom|side.chain
  src desc 2, 5.1

T S07 M run "All-atom RMSD on a 50-entry subset (validation)"
  help Recompute RMSD with all heavy atoms on 50 entries and compare with the Calpha ranking (Spearman); tells whether Calpha-only changes cluster order.
  meta wk=4 who=B ph=ext
  needs S04
  tool numpy, scipy
  out results/rmsd_allatom_subset.csv
  chk csv results/**/rmsd_allatom*.csv rows>=50
  src desc 5.1 step 2

T S08 S code "Hierarchical clustering at cuts 1.0 / 1.5 / 2.0 / 2.5 A"
  help Average linkage on the RMSD matrix; one label column per cut, plus the linkage saved for the dendrogram.
  meta wk=3 who=B ph=core
  needs S04 S05
  tool scipy
  out results/entry_clusters.csv
  chk csv results/**/*cluster*.csv rows>=300 cols=entry_id,cut_1.0,cut_1.5,cut_2.0,cut_2.5
  orig esr_analysis/cluster_structures.py
  src desc 5.1 step 3

T S09 XS code "Cluster statistics table"
  help Per cut: number of clusters, share of entries in the 3 largest clusters, median RMSD within and between clusters.
  meta wk=4 who=B ph=core
  needs S08
  out results/cluster_stats.csv
  chk csv results/**/cluster_stats*.csv rows>=4 cols=cut,n_clusters,top3_fraction
  src desc 5.1 report list

T S10 XS fig "Dendrogram"
  help Dendrogram of the linkage with the chosen cut drawn as a line.
  meta wk=4 who=B ph=core
  needs S08
  tool matplotlib, scipy
  out figures/dendrogram.png
  chk file figures/**/dendrogram*.png

T S11 S fig "PCA conformational landscape coloured by ligand class"
  help PCA of RMSD rows, axes with explained variance, points coloured agonist/antagonist/SERM/unknown; shows whether the landscape is multi-basin.
  meta wk=4 who=B ph=core
  needs S04 Q10
  tool scikit-learn, matplotlib
  out results/pca_coords.csv figures/pca_landscape_ligand_class.png
  chk csv results/**/pca*.csv rows>=300 cols=entry_id,pc1,pc2
  chk file figures/**/pca*class*.png
  orig esr_analysis/structural_pca.py

T S12 S code "Medoid structure per cluster"
  help For each cluster at the chosen cut, the entry with the smallest mean RMSD to its cluster mates.
  meta wk=4 who=B ph=core
  needs S08
  out results/medoids.csv
  chk csv results/**/medoid*.csv rows>=1 cols=cluster,entry_id
  orig esr_analysis/representative_set.py

T S13 S code "QC-conditioned reclustering (drop R-free > 0.30)"
  help Rerun clustering without failing entries and tabulate what changed (cluster count, top-3 share, lost clusters).
  meta wk=6 who=B ph=core
  needs S08 Q06
  out results/qc_clustering_delta.csv
  chk csv results/**/qc_cluster*delta*.csv rows>=1
  orig esr_analysis/compare_qc_clustering.py
  src desc 5.1 report list

T S14 XS fig "Threshold sensitivity figure"
  help Number of clusters and top-3 share as the cut moves from 1.0 to 2.5 A.
  meta wk=7 who=B ph=core
  needs S09
  out figures/structural_sensitivity.png
  chk file figures/**/structural_sensitivity*.png
  orig esr_analysis/plot_structural_sensitivity.py

T S15 S code "Minimal representative set covering >=90% of conformational diversity"
  help Smallest list of medoid entries (QC-pass if possible) whose clusters cover 90% of diversity, with a one-line justification per entry. If 90% is not reachable under QC, say so and show the number.
  meta wk=7 who=B ph=core
  needs S12 R04
  out results/representative_set.csv
  chk csv results/**/representative*.csv rows>=1 cols=entry_id,justification
  orig esr_analysis/representative_set.py
  src desc 10 deliverables

T S16 S code "Measure H12 position per entry after core fit"
  help RMSD (or displacement) of H12 residues 538-547 versus the reference after the core fit; this is the agonist/antagonist signal.
  meta wk=4 who=B ph=core
  needs S03
  out results/h12_metric.csv
  chk csv results/**/h12*.csv rows>=300 cols=entry_id,h12_rmsd
  src desc 3.2, 5.1

T S17 S run "Clean coordinate files: receptor chain + its ligand of interest"
  help Write one PDB per eligible chain with only that protein chain and its ligand(s) of interest (no waters, ions, additives, partner chains). For pockets (P2Rank), all-atom checks and PyMOL figures; the Calpha RMSD does not need it. Save the script in scripts/.
  meta wk=3 who=B ph=core
  needs Q18
  tool gemmi or biopython
  out data/clean/
  chk glob data/clean/*.pdb >=700
  chk cmd ! grep -lq "HOH" data/clean/*.pdb

# ===================== REDUNDANCY (phase core) =====================

T R01 XS code "Shannon entropy of the clustering, each cut"
  help Entropy (bits) of the cluster-size distribution at each cut; low = redundant dataset.
  meta wk=5 who=B ph=core
  needs S08
  tool scipy
  out results/entropy.csv
  chk csv results/**/entropy*.csv rows>=4 cols=cut,entropy_bits
  orig esr_analysis/cluster_entropy.py
  src desc 5.4

T R02 S code "Cumulative diversity curve (100 random orderings)"
  help For N = 1..total, mean and SD of clusters seen in a random sample of N structures; save the curve as CSV.
  meta wk=5 who=B ph=core
  needs S08
  out results/diversity_curve.csv
  chk csv results/**/diversity_curve*.csv rows>=300 cols=n,mean_clusters,sd_clusters
  orig esr_analysis/diversity_curve.py
  src desc 5.4

T R03 XS fig "Cumulative diversity figure with 90% line"
  help Plot R02 with a band and a dashed line at 90% of total diversity.
  meta wk=5 who=B ph=core
  needs R02
  out figures/diversity_curve.png
  chk file figures/**/diversity_curve*.png

T R04 XS code "90% saturation N at each cut"
  help The N where the mean curve reaches 90% of its maximum, for each of the 4 cuts.
  meta wk=5 who=B ph=core
  needs R02
  out results/saturation.csv
  chk csv results/**/saturation*.csv rows>=4 cols=cut,n_90

T R05 S code "Diversity curve per ligand class"
  help Repeat R02/R04 for agonist, antagonist, SERM separately; says which class is most redundant. Only valid if labels exist for enough entries; report n per class.
  meta wk=5 who=B ph=core
  needs R02 Q10
  out results/saturation_by_class.csv
  chk csv results/**/saturation_by_class*.csv rows>=1 cols=ligand_class,n_entries,n_90

T R06 XS code "Entropy with and without failing-QC entries"
  help Compare entropy and 90% N between the full set and the R-free<=0.30 set; answers whether QC changes the conclusion.
  meta wk=6 who=B ph=core
  needs R01 Q06 S13
  out results/entropy_qc_compare.csv
  chk csv results/**/entropy_qc*.csv rows>=2
  src desc 4.2 question 3

T R07 XS text "Plain-language answer to the central question"
  help Two paragraphs: how many structures are needed to capture 90% of ESR1 conformational diversity, by cut, and how much of the dataset is repetition. Every number must come from a results file.
  meta wk=8 who=B ph=core
  needs R04 R05 R06
  out docs/redundancy_answer.md
  chk lines docs/redundancy_answer.md >=6
  chk grep docs/redundancy_answer.md \d
  src desc 1, 5.4

# ===================== CHEMISTRY (phase core) =====================

T C01 XS code "RDKit parse check on all SMILES"
  help Parse every SMILES; write failures to a file so no ligand silently drops out.
  meta wk=2 who=C ph=core
  needs Q08
  tool rdkit
  out results/smiles_parse_report.csv
  chk csv results/**/smiles_parse*.csv rows>=1 cols=ligand_id,parsed

T C02 XS code "ECFP4 fingerprints (radius 2, 2048 bits)"
  help Morgan fingerprint per ligand, saved as an array with an id index.
  meta wk=2 who=C ph=core
  needs C01
  tool rdkit, numpy
  out results/fp_ecfp4.npy
  chk file results/**/fp_ecfp4*.npy
  orig esr_analysis/ligand_similarity.py

T C03 XS code "MACCS fingerprints (166 keys)"
  help MACCS key vector per ligand, saved like C02.
  meta wk=2 who=C ph=core
  needs C01
  tool rdkit, numpy
  out results/fp_maccs.npy
  chk file results/**/fp_maccs*.npy
  orig esr_analysis/ligand_similarity.py

T C04 XS code "Tanimoto similarity matrix - save to disk"
  help Pairwise Tanimoto on ECFP4; save with np.save.
  meta wk=3 who=C ph=core
  needs C02
  out results/tanimoto_ecfp4.npy
  chk npy results/**/tanimoto*.npy square>=300
  orig esr_analysis/ligand_similarity.py

T C05 S code "UMAP embedding of fingerprint space"
  help UMAP (Jaccard metric) of the fingerprints to 2D; log how many rows were finite.
  meta wk=4 who=C ph=core
  needs C02 C03
  tool umap-learn
  out results/umap_coords.csv
  chk csv results/**/umap*.csv rows>=300 cols=ligand_id,umap1,umap2
  orig esr_analysis/ligand_embedding.py

T C06 XS code "t-SNE embedding (optional comparison)"
  help t-SNE of the same fingerprints, to see whether UMAP structure is real.
  meta wk=4 who=C ph=ext
  needs C02
  out results/tsne_coords.csv
  chk csv results/**/tsne*.csv rows>=300

T C07 S code "K-means for K = 3..7 with silhouette scores"
  help Run K-means for each K and save silhouette (and BIC if easy) so K can be chosen with evidence.
  meta wk=3 who=C ph=core
  needs C02 C03
  tool scikit-learn
  out results/kmeans_scores.csv results/ligand_clusters.csv
  chk csv results/**/kmeans_scores*.csv rows>=5 cols=k,silhouette
  chk csv results/**/ligand_clusters*.csv rows>=300 cols=ligand_id,chem_cluster
  orig esr_analysis/cluster_ligands.py

T C10 S run "Rerun ECFP4 K-means on non-additive ligands only"
  help Keep only ligands where is_additive is false in results/ligands_ranked.csv, rerun K-means for K=3..7, save new scores and labels under new names. Keep the old files. Read ligand_id as text (keep_default_na=False).
  meta wk=7 who=C ph=core
  needs Q16 C07
  tool scikit-learn
  out results/ligand_clusters_noadd.csv
  out results/kmeans_scores_noadd.csv
  chk csv results/ligand_clusters_noadd.csv rows>=250 cols=ligand_id,chem_cluster nonempty=ligand_id uniq=ligand_id
  chk csv results/kmeans_scores_noadd.csv rows>=5 cols=k,silhouette

T C11 S run "Chemistry on ligands of interest only"
  help Rebuild the chemistry set as the distinct ligand_id values from results/chain_ligand_of_interest.csv (selected chains only), then recompute ECFP4, Tanimoto and K-means K=3..7 on that set. Keep the old files. Save the script in scripts/.
  meta wk=3 who=C ph=core
  needs Q18 C02
  tool rdkit, scikit-learn
  out results/ligands_of_interest.csv
  out results/kmeans_scores_loi.csv
  chk csv results/ligands_of_interest.csv rows>=150 cols=ligand_id,smiles,n_chains nonempty=ligand_id,smiles uniq=ligand_id
  chk csv results/kmeans_scores_loi.csv rows>=5 cols=k,silhouette
  chk glob scripts/*chem*.py >=1

T C08 XS decide "Choose K and write the reason"
  help Pick the K to use downstream from the non-additive clustering (C10) and state why (silhouette plus chemical sense); a human signs off.
  meta wk=7 who=C ph=core
  needs C07 C10 C11
  out docs/chemistry_k_choice.md
  chk grep docs/chemistry_k_choice.md (?i)silhouette
  chk man Human agrees with the chosen K

T C09 XS fig "UMAP figure by action type and cluster"
  help Two panels: coloured by K-means cluster and by action type (unknown shown in grey).
  meta wk=4 who=C ph=core
  needs C05 C08 Q10
  out figures/umap_ligands.png
  chk file figures/**/umap*.png

# ===================== LINKAGE (phase core) =====================

T L01 S code "Chemistry cluster vs action type test"
  help Contingency table chemistry cluster x action type (supported labels only) and a test; the earlier work found a link, reproduce it and state n.
  meta wk=5 who=C ph=core
  needs C08 Q10
  out results/link_chem_action.csv
  chk csv results/**/link_chem_action*.csv rows>=1 cols=statistic,n

T L02 S code "Chemistry cluster vs structural cluster contingency table"
  help Join each entry to its ligand's chemistry cluster and its structural cluster; save the table and the expected-count check (how many cells <5).
  meta wk=5 who=C ph=core
  needs C08 S08
  out results/link_chem_struct.csv
  chk csv results/**/link_chem_struct*.csv rows>=1
  orig esr_analysis/chemistry_structure_linkage.py

T L03 S code "p-values that are valid for sparse, dependent tables"
  help Entries from one study share ligand and crystal form, so a plain chi-square p is unreliable. Use a permutation or Monte-Carlo exact test (shuffle at ligand level), report the p-value and the caveat. Never leave p as None.
  meta wk=6 who=C ph=core
  needs L01 L02
  out results/link_tests.csv
  chk csv results/**/link_tests*.csv rows>=2 cols=test,p_value,method
  chk cmd ! grep -rlq --include='link_tests*.csv' None results
  orig esr_analysis/chemistry_structure_linkage.py (p was withheld there)
  src desc 5.3, 6.3 stats

T L04 S fig "Overlay chemistry clusters on the structural PCA"
  help PCA landscape (S11) with point colour = chemistry cluster and marker = action type; do chemistry clusters separate or interleave?
  meta wk=5 who=C ph=core
  needs S11 C08
  out figures/overlay_chem_on_pca.png
  chk file figures/**/overlay*.png
  src desc 5.3

T L05 S code "List disagreement cases"
  help Entries whose chemistry cluster and structural cluster do not match the dominant pairing; save as a table.
  meta wk=6 who=C ph=core
